WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:29.185
Beautiful dreamer, 
wake unto me,


00:02:30.359 --> 00:02:35.195
Starlight and dewdrops
are waiting for thee.


00:03:09.064 --> 00:03:10.430
Henry?


00:03:17.239 --> 00:03:18.355
Henry.


00:03:21.785 --> 00:03:23.071
Henry?


00:03:32.671 --> 00:03:33.878
Henry?


00:03:40.345 --> 00:03:42.177
Darling, what is it?


00:03:44.683 --> 00:03:46.390
What are you doing?


00:04:17.966 --> 00:04:20.208
He's coming for us.


00:04:56.171 --> 00:04:59.539
I couldn't move.
I started shaking.


00:04:59.633 --> 00:05:01.841
I was getting dizzy.


00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.758
I was sure everyone in the
room wanted to kill me.


00:05:12.646 --> 00:05:14.308
Ahhhh!


00:05:15.357 --> 00:05:17.565
I've never been so scared.


00:05:32.666 --> 00:05:35.283
Pointless in the
end though, fear, isn't it?


00:05:37.629 --> 00:05:39.666
That's your best advice, doc?


00:05:41.633 --> 00:05:43.465
Alright.


00:05:48.974 --> 00:05:51.057
What do you
think controls you?


00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:54.803
Eh? Your body or your mind?


00:05:56.106 --> 00:05:58.223
Your money controls me, sugar.


00:05:59.609 --> 00:06:02.272
Oh! There you go. Fine.


00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:03.398
Okay, okay.


00:06:03.488 --> 00:06:06.105
I think my body and
mind control each other.


00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:08.111
Well, let's find out.


00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:10.530
Is this real?


00:06:10.954 --> 00:06:11.865
Yes.


00:06:11.955 --> 00:06:13.241
- Yes?
- Yes.


00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:17.287
The mind is incredibly creative.


00:06:19.379 --> 00:06:25.592
It can make us see situations
that appear completely real,


00:06:27.512 --> 00:06:31.347
but are in fact nothing
more than illusions,


00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:35.972
perceptions of truth.


00:06:37.188 --> 00:06:38.429
How did you do that?


00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:44.777
Sometimes we all need a little
help to see the difference


00:06:44.863 --> 00:06:47.606
between reality and illusion.


00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:51.651
And that's about taking control,


00:06:51.745 --> 00:06:55.614
about not letting
fear control you.


00:06:57.876 --> 00:07:01.165
Because fear in the end
only exists in your mind.


00:07:04.341 --> 00:07:06.333
Mmm. Alright.


00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:08.258
Sorry to say goodnight.


00:07:11.181 --> 00:07:13.093
I'm
looking for Dr Price.


00:07:16.519 --> 00:07:19.512
I'm Arthur Gates, Chief Legal
Officer of the Winchester


00:07:19.606 --> 00:07:21.393
Repeating Arms Company.


00:07:21.483 --> 00:07:22.439
Really?


00:07:22.525 --> 00:07:24.357
See you next week, sugar.


00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:26.276
You're a hard man
to reach, Dr Price.


00:07:26.363 --> 00:07:27.319
Mm hmm.


00:07:27.405 --> 00:07:29.362
Goodnight, Nancy.


00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:31.156
- Goodnight.
- Goodnight.


00:07:32.702 --> 00:07:33.988
I'm on sabbatical.


00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:35.820
Goodnight!


00:07:37.749 --> 00:07:38.739
What do you want?


00:07:38.833 --> 00:07:39.789
A prescription?


00:07:39.876 --> 00:07:41.492
I've come to offer
you employment.


00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:43.960
Whiskey?


00:07:44.047 --> 00:07:45.629
Ah no, thank you.


00:07:46.424 --> 00:07:49.007
Are you familiar with Sarah
Winchester, Dr Price?


00:07:49.094 --> 00:07:52.383
Ah Mrs Winchester's husband,
William, was the majority


00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:55.965
shareholder of the Winchester
Repeating Arms Company.


00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:00.269
25 years ago, William passed,
leaving Mrs Winchester a rather


00:08:00.355 --> 00:08:04.099
large inheritance, and 51
percent of the company.


00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:08.482
Mrs Winchester also lost
her only child, Annie.


00:08:10.615 --> 00:08:13.699
It's said in her grief,
she turned to a medium


00:08:13.785 --> 00:08:16.277
spiritualist of some sort.


00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.414
The medium may have taken
advantage of her mental state.


00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.867
That's not uncommon
after a tragedy.


00:08:22.961 --> 00:08:26.250
I can assure you, Sarah
Winchester is anything


00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:27.796
but common.


00:08:28.967 --> 00:08:31.425
Aye, after her spiritual
encounter, she moved across the


00:08:31.511 --> 00:08:34.345
country to San Jose, where
she purchased what was...


00:08:34.431 --> 00:08:37.094
- Where's my-
- ...then an eight room house.


00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.594
Maybe it's in the garden room.


00:08:38.685 --> 00:08:41.302
She spent the last 20
years expanding it.


00:08:41.396 --> 00:08:46.437
Wh-what stands now is a ah
gargantuan seven storeyed


00:08:46.526 --> 00:08:50.691
structure, with no apparent
rhyme or reason, no master plan,


00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:55.024
each maze of halls more
confusing than the next.


00:08:56.286 --> 00:08:58.653
A house under never-ending
construction, built on the


00:08:58.747 --> 00:09:03.208
orders of a grieving widow,
whose mind is as chaotic


00:09:03.293 --> 00:09:05.000
as the house itself.


00:09:05.086 --> 00:09:07.999
Over the years, she's become
more and more reclusive.


00:09:08.089 --> 00:09:11.548
Last month, the Board of
Directors enacted its right to


00:09:11.634 --> 00:09:15.878
assess Mrs Winchester's state
of mind, to determine if she's


00:09:15.972 --> 00:09:17.429
fit to control the company.


00:09:18.475 --> 00:09:20.717
You want to take
it away from her?


00:09:21.728 --> 00:09:24.311
We're worried about
her sanity, Dr Price.


00:09:26.232 --> 00:09:28.315
We need a professional.


00:09:29.819 --> 00:09:32.732
Any kind of diagnosis from
such a long distance


00:09:32.822 --> 00:09:34.279
would be impossible.


00:09:34.365 --> 00:09:36.982
Well, Mrs Winchester has
agreed to let you stay at the


00:09:37.077 --> 00:09:40.161
residence, an offer
that is exceedingly rare.


00:09:42.916 --> 00:09:45.124
An unwilling patient,
the long distance.


00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.042
This is, this is, this is
not something ordinarily I...


00:09:47.128 --> 00:09:48.118
Name the amount.


00:09:48.213 --> 00:09:49.294
Doesn't really work like that.


00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:50.791
How much do you owe?


00:09:52.258 --> 00:09:53.169
Mortgage?


00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:55.171
Hospital expenses?


00:09:56.763 --> 00:09:57.970
Medicine?


00:09:59.182 --> 00:10:00.218
Three hundred.


00:10:00.308 --> 00:10:01.890
We'll pay six...


00:10:02.769 --> 00:10:04.385
for the appropriate assessment.


00:10:52.986 --> 00:10:56.104
Mrs Winchester
requests the bay window frame be


00:10:56.197 --> 00:10:58.109
installed by sundown.


00:10:58.199 --> 00:10:59.781
Move with haste.


00:11:09.502 --> 00:11:11.368
Let me get that, sir.


00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:13.370
Thank you.


00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.002
Busy day of
construction here, sir.


00:11:20.096 --> 00:11:21.007
Yes.


00:11:21.097 --> 00:11:22.884
Days and nights are
always busy here.


00:11:22.974 --> 00:11:24.431
Really? Nights, too?


00:11:24.517 --> 00:11:27.385
Right round the clock, sir.
This way.


00:11:30.064 --> 00:11:32.477
Most of the the rooms
don't stay up very long,


00:11:32.567 --> 00:11:35.605
like Mrs Winchester's
garden room there.


00:11:36.237 --> 00:11:37.773
That might not last the season.


00:11:38.698 --> 00:11:39.734
Really?


00:11:41.993 --> 00:11:44.076
Please wait in
the library, sir.


00:11:44.162 --> 00:11:46.245
I'll call for Mrs Marriot.


00:12:43.096 --> 00:12:44.507
Jesus!


00:12:44.597 --> 00:12:45.713
My apologies, sir.


00:12:45.807 --> 00:12:47.514
The door was making
a terrible racket.


00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:50.308
No, no, no, no, no.
That's quite alright.


00:12:51.312 --> 00:12:52.598
Gave me a fright.


00:13:00.488 --> 00:13:01.569
Dr Price?


00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:03.151
Yes.


00:13:03.241 --> 00:13:05.278
Welcome. Marion Marriott,
Mrs Winchester's niece.


00:13:05.368 --> 00:13:08.202
Oh, well, it's a
pleasure to meet you.


00:13:08.288 --> 00:13:11.656
I must say, I have never
quite seen a house like this.


00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:14.913
My aunt advised me of
the nature of your visit.


00:13:16.129 --> 00:13:17.870
As you are aware, it is
unfortunate timing, so I would


00:13:17.964 --> 00:13:20.331
ask you to behave in a manner
befitting the circumstance.


00:13:20.425 --> 00:13:21.882
Unfortunate, how?


00:13:21.968 --> 00:13:23.550
A tragedy occurred.


00:13:23.636 --> 00:13:26.379
Oh. Well,
I'm sorry to hear that.


00:13:26.472 --> 00:13:28.054
Are you carrying firearms?


00:13:29.309 --> 00:13:30.390
Should I be?


00:13:30.476 --> 00:13:31.717
Aunt Sarah forbids them.


00:13:31.811 --> 00:13:33.222
Well!


00:13:33.313 --> 00:13:35.805
I'm ah completely unarmed.


00:13:36.441 --> 00:13:37.807
Good.


00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:40.517
You, like I, like everyone, are
guests in Aunt Sarah's home.


00:13:40.611 --> 00:13:41.772
You will abide by her rules.


00:13:41.863 --> 00:13:43.104
Understood.


00:13:43.197 --> 00:13:45.405
You are to stay in this section
of the house, the east wing.


00:13:45.491 --> 00:13:47.403
Aunt Sarah's private
domains are off limits.


00:13:47.493 --> 00:13:48.609
Understood.


00:13:49.579 --> 00:13:52.617
So ah, are you
close to your aunt?


00:13:52.707 --> 00:13:55.370
Is this already part of
your evaluation, Dr Price?


00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:56.826
Oh no, Ma'am, it is not.


00:13:57.712 --> 00:13:58.873
Yes.


00:13:58.963 --> 00:14:01.046
Aunt Sarah is an exceptional
woman. She does not deserve


00:14:01.132 --> 00:14:03.590
to be treated with anything
less than complete respect.


00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:05.967
Yes, Ma'am. Quite right.


00:14:13.102 --> 00:14:14.343
May I?


00:14:17.899 --> 00:14:19.561
This is the grand ballroom,


00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:21.516
built almost entirely
without nails.


00:14:21.611 --> 00:14:24.524
The walls and parquet floor are
made of six separate hardwoods.


00:14:25.406 --> 00:14:27.898
The silver chandelier was
imported from Germany.


00:14:33.998 --> 00:14:35.239
Follow me, doctor.


00:14:36.042 --> 00:14:37.749
There are almost one
hundred rooms in the house.


00:14:37.835 --> 00:14:39.417
It's easy to get lost.


00:15:11.077 --> 00:15:13.535
How ah unusual!


00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.287
Aunt Sarah suffers
from arthritis.


00:15:16.374 --> 00:15:18.536
This makes climbing stairs
manageable for her.


00:15:18.626 --> 00:15:20.834
The house can be overwhelming.
Do keep up.


00:15:27.969 --> 00:15:29.460
What is this?


00:15:30.888 --> 00:15:32.550
It's a communication device.


00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.006
Really?


00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:36.387
You speak into the holes and
a series of pipes travel the


00:15:36.477 --> 00:15:38.514
sound to the desired room.


00:15:42.942 --> 00:15:43.978
Ha!


00:15:44.944 --> 00:15:46.606
Ingenious.
- Yes.


00:15:46.696 --> 00:15:49.029
You'll find many of my aunt's
inventions are state-of-the-art.


00:15:49.115 --> 00:15:51.482
I trust you'll find everything
you need with the room.


00:15:52.452 --> 00:15:54.284
Aunt Sarah will be
joining us for dinner.


00:15:55.329 --> 00:15:57.537
Perhaps you would like to
freshen up beforehand.


00:15:57.623 --> 00:15:59.785
I very much look forward
to meeting your aunt.


00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.452
Aunt Sarah would not approve of
you drinking before dinner hour.


00:16:03.546 --> 00:16:06.960
Her sense of smell is
still as acute as mine.


00:16:08.718 --> 00:16:10.254
Respect her wishes.


00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.393
You were right about me, Ruby.


00:16:27.945 --> 00:16:29.356
I am...


00:16:31.866 --> 00:16:33.198
a fraud.


00:16:49.425 --> 00:16:51.633
You're a phony, mm?


00:16:56.182 --> 00:16:57.764
Oh, that feels good!


00:17:02.563 --> 00:17:04.805
Well, you don't
know what you're doing.


00:17:09.487 --> 00:17:12.025
You don't know
what you're doing.


00:17:12.114 --> 00:17:14.697
Oh yeah.
You prove nothing.


00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:18.577
Ahhh.


00:17:22.291 --> 00:17:24.203
For Christ's sake.


00:17:28.089 --> 00:17:29.921
Christ!


00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:16.422
Who are you?
What do you want?


00:18:16.512 --> 00:18:18.970
Dinner will be
served in ten minutes.


00:18:19.432 --> 00:18:21.469
You're ah, you're alone, yes?


00:18:21.559 --> 00:18:22.549
Yes, sir.


00:18:22.643 --> 00:18:23.679
Nobody else with you?


00:18:23.769 --> 00:18:24.759
No, sir.


00:18:24.854 --> 00:18:26.641
No? You didn't see anyone
just come out of here?


00:18:26.731 --> 00:18:28.188
Are you alright, sir?


00:18:30.568 --> 00:18:32.730
I'm fine. I just
thought someone else was-


00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:35.483
Well, I thought I saw
someone else in my room. Ha!


00:18:36.907 --> 00:18:38.148
Interesting.


00:18:38.242 --> 00:18:40.859
Hmm. Look, I'm fine, yes.
Dinner in ten minutes, yes?


00:18:41.329 --> 00:18:42.240
Sir.


00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:43.616
Good, thank you.


00:18:50.379 --> 00:18:51.745
Take
it nice and easy.


00:18:53.841 --> 00:18:55.548
Phew! There.


00:19:13.027 --> 00:19:14.143
Henry!


00:19:14.945 --> 00:19:16.152
Stop it!


00:19:25.414 --> 00:19:26.825
Henry, stop that!


00:19:29.126 --> 00:19:29.991
Henry!


00:19:30.836 --> 00:19:32.202
Henry! Just-


00:19:34.548 --> 00:19:37.416
Henry, you must be very
excited to spend some time in


00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:39.376
your great aunt's house.


00:19:40.388 --> 00:19:42.596
We're here because father died.


00:19:46.435 --> 00:19:48.597
Well, I am very sorry
for your loss, young man.


00:19:49.188 --> 00:19:50.019
I'm not.


00:19:50.106 --> 00:19:51.222
Henry!


00:19:51.315 --> 00:19:53.682
It's my fault.
I didn't mean to pry.


00:19:54.777 --> 00:19:56.985
Of course you did.
That's why you're here.


00:19:58.364 --> 00:19:59.775
Yes.


00:19:59.865 --> 00:20:01.322
Suppose so.


00:20:01.867 --> 00:20:04.200
I recently lost someone myself.


00:20:04.286 --> 00:20:06.448
So if you feel like discussing
anything, I might be able to


00:20:06.539 --> 00:20:10.624
provide some assistance to
yourself or young Henry here.


00:20:12.503 --> 00:20:16.042
I imagine you must be very
good at your job if Aunt Sarah


00:20:16.132 --> 00:20:17.668
chose you to be her assessor.


00:20:20.636 --> 00:20:22.878
I had no idea she
chose me herself.


00:20:22.972 --> 00:20:24.508
I'm just hoping that I can help.


00:20:24.598 --> 00:20:27.591
If you want to help, doctor, you
can give my aunt a clean bill


00:20:27.685 --> 00:20:29.768
of health and be on your way.


00:20:30.604 --> 00:20:32.846
Well, I have a duty to my
profession and an obligation


00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:34.272
to my employers.


00:20:35.609 --> 00:20:37.521
Aunt Sarah is your employer.


00:20:38.821 --> 00:20:40.608
It is still half her company.


00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:55.911
Madam!


00:21:02.178 --> 00:21:03.294
Good evening, madam.


00:21:38.297 --> 00:21:39.708
Dr Price.


00:21:39.799 --> 00:21:42.212
Mrs Winchester, it's a
pleasure to finally meet you.


00:21:42.301 --> 00:21:44.293
The pleasure is due to the
lawyers of the Winchester


00:21:44.386 --> 00:21:46.093
Repeating Arms Company.


00:21:48.349 --> 00:21:49.385
Yes.


00:21:49.475 --> 00:21:51.137
That's probably right.


00:21:52.436 --> 00:21:55.019
I hope everything has been
to your satisfaction so far?


00:21:55.105 --> 00:21:57.222
I cannot fault the hospitality.


00:21:57.316 --> 00:22:00.400
It's quite a special
house, is it not?


00:22:01.529 --> 00:22:04.442
Now that, Ma'am, is a
fact beyond dispute.


00:22:07.159 --> 00:22:08.366
Thank you.


00:22:10.496 --> 00:22:13.034
I understand the Winchester is
still considered the superior


00:22:13.123 --> 00:22:14.910
rifle on the market, Ma'am.


00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:16.332
Superior?


00:22:18.045 --> 00:22:19.627
Superior at what?


00:22:20.923 --> 00:22:23.882
Accuracy, range, stopping power.


00:22:23.968 --> 00:22:25.004
Killing.


00:22:25.094 --> 00:22:27.177
Indiscriminate killing.


00:22:28.597 --> 00:22:30.054
Very superior.


00:22:30.641 --> 00:22:33.930
You feel responsible for
the misuse of your product?


00:22:35.062 --> 00:22:38.226
If a weapon works as intended,
one can hardly call it a misuse.


00:22:38.315 --> 00:22:40.682
Well, it can
be used for good or bad,


00:22:40.776 --> 00:22:42.768
depending on the
person wielding it.


00:22:45.698 --> 00:22:46.939
Yes.


00:22:48.033 --> 00:22:50.070
Then again, perhaps
roller-skates are a less


00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:51.401
dangerous endeavor.


00:22:51.495 --> 00:22:55.205
The company is expanding,
looking for other opportunities.


00:22:55.291 --> 00:22:57.704
I understand that was at
your behest, Mrs Winchester?


00:22:57.793 --> 00:23:00.331
It was.
To the displeasure of the board.


00:23:00.421 --> 00:23:04.415
It appears that strapping wheels
to one's feet can also be a,


00:23:04.508 --> 00:23:06.420
a perilous endeavor.


00:23:09.013 --> 00:23:10.220
Hear, hear.


00:23:30.284 --> 00:23:32.867
Tell me the
story about the farmer


00:23:32.953 --> 00:23:34.569
who owned the old mule.


00:23:34.663 --> 00:23:35.494
No.


00:23:35.581 --> 00:23:37.538
I always liked that story.


00:23:38.751 --> 00:23:41.243
- A delusional disorder.
- Yes.


00:23:41.337 --> 00:23:43.078
- That's what you called it.
- Yes.


00:23:44.381 --> 00:23:47.340
I don't want to talk anymore.
I need you to believe me.


00:23:47.426 --> 00:23:49.918
I want to be with you, Ruby.


00:23:50.012 --> 00:23:51.594
Together forever.


00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:22.167
Hello?


00:24:36.308 --> 00:24:37.970
Hello?


00:25:18.684 --> 00:25:19.674
Ah!


00:27:12.464 --> 00:27:13.875
Oh! Christ!


00:27:20.097 --> 00:27:22.089
Oh, you've poisoned
your mind, Eric;


00:27:22.182 --> 00:27:23.798
you've poisoned your mind!


00:27:23.892 --> 00:27:25.508
I need some air.


00:28:47.184 --> 00:28:49.517
Ohhh! Ohhh! Déjà-vu!


00:29:11.250 --> 00:29:11.990
Hey!


00:30:21.361 --> 00:30:22.067
Hey!


00:30:24.364 --> 00:30:25.775
Hey!!


00:30:26.616 --> 00:30:27.402
Move, hey!


00:30:27.492 --> 00:30:28.653
Move! Move!


00:30:30.037 --> 00:30:31.118
Ahhh!


00:30:31.788 --> 00:30:33.245
Ohhh!


00:30:37.085 --> 00:30:38.701
I see you!


00:30:44.092 --> 00:30:45.173
Oh! Henry!


00:30:45.260 --> 00:30:46.171
Darling!


00:30:49.056 --> 00:30:51.298
What's happening
to you, sweetheart?


00:30:52.059 --> 00:30:53.266
Ohhh!


00:30:56.897 --> 00:30:58.229
Thank you.


00:31:02.235 --> 00:31:04.352
Darling, what's
happening to you?


00:31:09.868 --> 00:31:13.407
Mrs Winchester, I really
must have your full attention.


00:31:13.497 --> 00:31:15.284
Oh, you have it, Dr Price.


00:31:15.374 --> 00:31:18.492
Yes, but perhaps you would
be more comfortable if-


00:31:18.585 --> 00:31:20.622
Last night was quite
a traumatic event.


00:31:20.712 --> 00:31:22.954
I'm grateful for your actions.


00:31:23.048 --> 00:31:27.713
I fear you may have me at a, an
emotional disadvantage today.


00:31:27.803 --> 00:31:29.260
Yes, I understand.


00:31:29.346 --> 00:31:31.884
I don't mean to pry, but has
Master Henry been prone to


00:31:31.973 --> 00:31:33.680
sleepwalking in the past?


00:31:34.768 --> 00:31:35.758
No.


00:31:36.978 --> 00:31:39.436
But you may know, he did witness
the death of his father.


00:31:40.232 --> 00:31:41.143
Yes.


00:31:43.944 --> 00:31:46.482
Well, this is the first in
a series of sessions I wish


00:31:46.571 --> 00:31:49.655
to conduct. And I can assure you
that today will be quite benign.


00:31:49.741 --> 00:31:52.358
No, no, no. Let's just get
straight to it, doctor.


00:31:52.452 --> 00:31:55.695
You are here to assess my
erratic behavior, are you not?


00:31:55.789 --> 00:31:57.746
Well, erratic behavior
is not the phrase that


00:31:57.833 --> 00:31:58.823
I would've chosen, but-


00:31:58.917 --> 00:32:00.624
No, I will
speak with you truthfully.


00:32:00.710 --> 00:32:01.621
Please.


00:32:01.711 --> 00:32:02.997
But you will do me
the same courtesy.


00:32:03.088 --> 00:32:04.169
Of course.


00:32:04.256 --> 00:32:06.794
Do you suffer from
soldier's syndrome?


00:32:07.342 --> 00:32:08.298
I'm sorry?


00:32:08.385 --> 00:32:10.968
Are you an abuser of medication?


00:32:12.097 --> 00:32:14.430
Mrs Winchester, I think it's
best if I ask the questions.


00:32:14.516 --> 00:32:17.179
Your wife, did she believe
you are a good therapist?


00:32:17.269 --> 00:32:19.101
We're not here to
discuss my wife.


00:32:19.187 --> 00:32:20.723
Your wife, Ruby?


00:32:23.191 --> 00:32:27.105
No, we are not. And I would
appreciate your honesty.


00:32:27.195 --> 00:32:29.687
Are you an abuser of medication?
- No, I'm not.


00:32:36.329 --> 00:32:37.786
So.


00:32:37.873 --> 00:32:39.910
I will share a fact with you,
which you may find questionable.


00:32:40.000 --> 00:32:42.083
But I assure you, it is a fact.


00:32:42.169 --> 00:32:43.250
Please.


00:32:43.336 --> 00:32:45.328
I am cursed.


00:32:45.422 --> 00:32:47.038
Cursed, how?


00:32:47.132 --> 00:32:48.839
Have you read my papers?


00:32:48.925 --> 00:32:50.541
- Of course I have.
- And what did they say?


00:32:50.635 --> 00:32:53.173
Well, among many things, they
say that this is the house


00:32:53.263 --> 00:32:54.629
that spirits built.


00:32:54.723 --> 00:32:58.182
See, profiting from such a
thing as violence and death,


00:32:58.268 --> 00:33:03.104
oh, that is a wickedness that
follows you like a shadow.


00:33:04.191 --> 00:33:06.399
Yes, we might also call
those shadows 'guilt'.


00:33:07.152 --> 00:33:09.610
But tell me, how do
these shadows follow you?


00:33:09.696 --> 00:33:12.313
I may be getting old,
Dr Price, but I assure you,


00:33:12.407 --> 00:33:13.864
I have not lost my senses.


00:33:13.950 --> 00:33:17.239
I know the difference between
illusion and reality.


00:33:18.330 --> 00:33:19.366
I see.


00:33:22.501 --> 00:33:24.367
Your mind rules your body.


00:33:26.004 --> 00:33:28.087
The mind can be
incredibly creative.


00:33:28.173 --> 00:33:32.008
But it can also,
at times, fail us.


00:33:32.093 --> 00:33:34.176
My mind has never failed me.


00:33:34.262 --> 00:33:39.053
What we see, taste and
touch are interpreted and


00:33:39.142 --> 00:33:41.350
processed to give us our truth.


00:33:41.436 --> 00:33:44.395
And that truth can
in turn be an illusion,


00:33:44.481 --> 00:33:47.849
created, distorted, by grief.


00:33:52.322 --> 00:33:54.564
Do you believe in
ghosts, Dr Price?


00:33:55.283 --> 00:33:57.195
No, Ma'am. Why would I?


00:33:58.036 --> 00:34:00.995
Offering my staff that bill
would be greatly appreciated.


00:34:01.081 --> 00:34:04.574
Even the nickel inside the bill
would be a respectable start.


00:34:07.254 --> 00:34:08.836
Oh really!
Silly illusions!


00:34:08.922 --> 00:34:10.709
Do you take me for a fool?


00:34:10.799 --> 00:34:11.789
No, Ma'am. I do not.


00:34:11.883 --> 00:34:13.795
No more diversions from reality.


00:34:13.885 --> 00:34:15.092
No more parlor tricks.


00:34:15.178 --> 00:34:17.636
And your medication will
have to be confiscated.


00:34:17.722 --> 00:34:20.180
Mrs Winchester, I'm sorry, but
I must insist, I'm not a child...


00:34:20.267 --> 00:34:21.348
This is my home, Dr Price.


00:34:21.434 --> 00:34:24.222
And I will not be...
- You will obey my rules.


00:34:25.605 --> 00:34:28.689
If you want me to open up this
house for you, you need clarity.


00:34:32.696 --> 00:34:34.733
Do you have another
question for me?


00:34:36.741 --> 00:34:38.198
Yes, Ma'am.


00:34:42.372 --> 00:34:45.160
Is it really necessary to
confine me to quarters?


00:34:45.250 --> 00:34:47.537
It is Madam's wish, sir.


00:34:48.420 --> 00:34:49.752
Hmmm.


00:34:49.838 --> 00:34:52.000
And the condition
of Master Henry?


00:34:52.090 --> 00:34:54.628
He too is confined to quarters.


00:34:54.718 --> 00:34:57.131
And Mrs Marriott has
not left his side.


00:35:27.042 --> 00:35:28.158
Dammit!


00:35:41.473 --> 00:35:44.511
Sir, the members of the board
eagerly await your evaluation.


00:35:44.601 --> 00:35:46.558
I trust you will make
an accurate assessment.


00:35:46.645 --> 00:35:49.058
Regards, Arthur C Gates,
Chief Legal Officer.


00:36:00.784 --> 00:36:03.492
Sarah Winchester's
psychological assessment and


00:36:03.578 --> 00:36:05.365
mental status examination.


00:36:05.455 --> 00:36:09.244
Dr Eric A Price, April 16, 1906.


00:36:10.126 --> 00:36:12.584
Appearance, normal.


00:36:12.671 --> 00:36:15.209
Hygiene, physical
characteristics, all normal.


00:36:15.298 --> 00:36:18.291
Patient struggles with the
loss of her husband and child.


00:36:18.385 --> 00:36:21.253
Her behavior is at times
slightly aggressive.


00:36:21.346 --> 00:36:24.384
Perception, visual
hallucinations that patient


00:36:24.474 --> 00:36:27.137
often refers to as
shadows or ghosts.


00:36:29.270 --> 00:36:32.229
I feel them, their presence.


00:36:40.573 --> 00:36:41.689
Go on.


00:36:46.454 --> 00:36:49.197
I feel their presence,
their energy.


00:36:50.250 --> 00:36:53.209
Their unfinished business
has brought them here.


00:36:54.546 --> 00:36:56.458
Do you perhaps in any way blame
them for the death of your


00:36:56.548 --> 00:36:58.039
husband and child?


00:36:58.133 --> 00:37:02.127
I will mourn William
and dear Annie always.


00:37:02.220 --> 00:37:05.930
I love all my family
very much, Dr Price.


00:37:06.015 --> 00:37:08.382
They are the true
riches of my life,


00:37:08.476 --> 00:37:11.685
and I will do whatever
it takes to protect them.


00:37:26.411 --> 00:37:29.449
Can you tell me why ah, why
those bells chime at midnight?


00:37:29.539 --> 00:37:31.451
It's midnight, sir.


00:37:32.083 --> 00:37:33.164
Well, yes.


00:37:33.251 --> 00:37:36.585
But is there any
significance to it?


00:37:37.380 --> 00:37:39.212
It's midnight, sir.


00:37:43.344 --> 00:37:44.380
Thank you.


00:41:06.172 --> 00:41:08.539
I swear, the laudanum
is still in my system.


00:41:08.633 --> 00:41:10.124
Ahhh, ahhh.


00:41:10.218 --> 00:41:13.427
Let's just hope
it's withdrawals.


00:41:13.513 --> 00:41:16.472
It always was withdrawals
- it had to be.


00:41:16.557 --> 00:41:18.423
Had to be.


00:41:21.896 --> 00:41:24.354
I have a question
for you, Dr Price.


00:41:24.440 --> 00:41:26.056
Again, Mrs Winchester,
it's best if I ask-


00:41:26.150 --> 00:41:27.891
What is it like to die?


00:41:27.986 --> 00:41:29.067
Talking about your...


00:41:29.153 --> 00:41:31.770
Deceased for three
minutes, were you not?


00:41:35.493 --> 00:41:38.952
You know, I keep records


00:41:39.038 --> 00:41:41.872
of all the lives a
Winchester has taken.


00:41:43.334 --> 00:41:46.418
Hundreds have been reported;
probably thousands haven't.


00:41:48.172 --> 00:41:52.041
The guilty, the innocent - the
rifle doesn't discriminate.


00:41:52.135 --> 00:41:55.299
And many of the souls make
their way to this house.


00:41:55.388 --> 00:41:56.879
That's impressive.


00:41:58.141 --> 00:42:00.679
As you can clearly see,
I am still here. So perhaps


00:42:00.768 --> 00:42:03.681
you could do me the kindness
of taking me off that shelf.


00:42:04.856 --> 00:42:06.518
You were shot.


00:42:06.607 --> 00:42:08.018
I was.


00:42:14.824 --> 00:42:15.985
This.


00:42:17.285 --> 00:42:19.026
And it did kill me.


00:42:23.916 --> 00:42:26.829
You kept it and refurbished it.


00:42:27.712 --> 00:42:28.998
I did.


00:42:29.088 --> 00:42:30.124
Why?


00:42:30.214 --> 00:42:32.672
Well, because it's a
reminder of my past.


00:42:32.759 --> 00:42:37.049
Because it's my connection to
death and to all that I've lost.


00:42:39.348 --> 00:42:42.011
Instruments of death
have a powerful connection


00:42:42.101 --> 00:42:43.717
to the afterlife.


00:42:46.647 --> 00:42:49.890
We hold onto mementoes
to help us heal.


00:42:49.984 --> 00:42:52.727
But sometimes, they do
more harm than good.


00:42:52.820 --> 00:42:54.231
Precisely.


00:42:54.322 --> 00:42:57.815
So tell me, what do you think
it is you're holding onto?


00:43:01.662 --> 00:43:03.824
Have you ever been
to a spiritualist?


00:43:05.333 --> 00:43:07.325
But I understand you have.


00:43:07.418 --> 00:43:10.252
You know, it is believed that
once we've departed this world,


00:43:10.338 --> 00:43:14.708
we can see others who have left
their physical selves behind.


00:43:14.801 --> 00:43:15.962
Is that right?


00:43:16.052 --> 00:43:18.669
Have you ever
experienced such a thing?


00:43:18.763 --> 00:43:21.050
I can't say that I have, no.


00:43:21.766 --> 00:43:23.928
Is it painful to die?


00:43:24.977 --> 00:43:27.720
Mrs Winchester, w-we really must
continue with this evaluation.


00:43:27.814 --> 00:43:29.726
Please, doctor. Please.


00:43:29.816 --> 00:43:31.057
Yes.


00:43:33.778 --> 00:43:35.360
And then nothing.


00:43:37.490 --> 00:43:39.106
Just a calmness.


00:43:40.118 --> 00:43:43.156
And when I came back,
it was painful again.


00:43:44.622 --> 00:43:46.579
If that makes sense.


00:43:47.500 --> 00:43:48.741
Yes.


00:43:52.088 --> 00:43:55.001
Yes, because you too have
experienced great pain.


00:43:56.175 --> 00:44:00.260
Oh, grief can be far more
crippling than arthritis,


00:44:00.346 --> 00:44:01.553
doctor.


00:44:01.639 --> 00:44:04.632
Mrs Winchester, do you blame the
shadows for the loss of your


00:44:04.725 --> 00:44:06.512
husband and child?


00:44:08.479 --> 00:44:10.812
Were you out of your
room last night?


00:44:15.653 --> 00:44:17.485
Yes, I was.


00:44:18.281 --> 00:44:19.692
Thank you.


00:44:19.782 --> 00:44:22.024
Thank you for
telling me the truth.


00:44:32.837 --> 00:44:35.170
So, why all the noise?


00:44:35.256 --> 00:44:37.043
Why all this construction?


00:44:37.133 --> 00:44:39.216
They want me to build, doctor.


00:44:39.302 --> 00:44:44.138
The spirits killed by
the rifle, they guide me.


00:44:45.474 --> 00:44:48.262
Guide you in drawing
building plans?


00:44:48.352 --> 00:44:49.468
Yes.


00:44:50.605 --> 00:44:52.016
What? Why?


00:44:52.106 --> 00:44:55.099
For the rooms, of course.
You see, once their


00:44:55.193 --> 00:44:58.311
rooms are completed, their
presence grows stronger.


00:44:59.655 --> 00:45:01.817
Hence the house
that spirits built?


00:45:01.908 --> 00:45:03.274
Yes.


00:45:04.118 --> 00:45:08.078
The shadows that follow me,
they have unfinished business.


00:45:08.956 --> 00:45:11.323
You saw what I did
last night, didn't you?


00:45:12.043 --> 00:45:13.500
I did.


00:45:14.587 --> 00:45:16.954
At the chime of
midnight, they clamor.


00:45:18.257 --> 00:45:20.214
The bells summon them.


00:45:21.344 --> 00:45:25.304
They communicate
through plans, drawings.


00:45:26.599 --> 00:45:29.933
They want me to reconstruct
the rooms that they died in,


00:45:30.019 --> 00:45:32.602
then they can enter our world.


00:45:33.522 --> 00:45:35.138
And the trouble is, I
don't always know who it is


00:45:35.233 --> 00:45:38.021
I'm speaking with.
I-it could be some innocent


00:45:38.110 --> 00:45:42.400
bystander or, or
a victim of a crime, or...


00:45:45.952 --> 00:45:47.534
someone else.


00:45:47.620 --> 00:45:49.532
Who else, Mrs Winchester?


00:45:50.623 --> 00:45:54.287
Last night, a spirit more
powerful than any I've


00:45:54.377 --> 00:45:57.620
encountered
endangered my family.


00:45:59.757 --> 00:46:01.339
Who are you?


00:46:03.052 --> 00:46:07.763
Doctor, who do you see in
this room at this moment?


00:46:08.432 --> 00:46:09.843
Just you.


00:46:11.769 --> 00:46:12.805
Only me?


00:46:22.697 --> 00:46:24.063
Just you.


00:46:25.199 --> 00:46:26.906
It will take time.


00:46:27.535 --> 00:46:29.618
You still need to
clear your head.


00:46:49.390 --> 00:46:50.722
Oh, sir!


00:46:51.642 --> 00:46:53.634
I would like to check in on
Mrs Marriott and Master Henry,


00:46:53.728 --> 00:46:54.388
if I may.


00:46:54.478 --> 00:46:56.185
I will enquire, sir.


00:46:56.272 --> 00:46:58.889
Perhaps, may I ask
you a question?


00:46:59.942 --> 00:47:01.058
Question, sir?


00:47:01.152 --> 00:47:04.987
Yes. I mean tell me, have you
ever seen any, any ghosts?


00:47:06.073 --> 00:47:07.905
No, sir.


00:47:09.035 --> 00:47:12.028
But you have heard the
rumors, the stories?


00:47:12.121 --> 00:47:14.784
I have heard tall tales.


00:47:15.374 --> 00:47:17.741
Some taller than others.


00:47:18.919 --> 00:47:21.502
Have you ever witnessed
anything out of the ordinary?


00:47:29.055 --> 00:47:33.015
So display cabinets along the
walls and then a line of them


00:47:33.100 --> 00:47:34.682
down the middle of the room.


00:47:34.769 --> 00:47:36.635
Yes, Ma'am.


00:47:36.729 --> 00:47:39.938
And ah what type of Winchester
would you like delivered?


00:47:41.859 --> 00:47:44.226
Every type, every model.


00:47:46.697 --> 00:47:48.438
Okay, let's go back.


00:47:49.325 --> 00:47:52.159
Tell me please what happens
once these rooms are finished?


00:47:52.244 --> 00:47:55.954
Well, the spirit's presence
grows more powerful and


00:47:56.040 --> 00:47:57.872
more... more focused.


00:47:57.958 --> 00:48:00.291
Their voices get stronger.


00:48:00.378 --> 00:48:01.494
And we converse.


00:48:01.587 --> 00:48:04.079
Converse how? About what?


00:48:04.173 --> 00:48:07.041
I show them my deep remorse.


00:48:08.386 --> 00:48:11.754
I want to help them let go of
their grief and their anger.


00:48:11.847 --> 00:48:13.133
And how do they react?


00:48:13.224 --> 00:48:14.635
Favorably.


00:48:14.725 --> 00:48:16.591
Yes, mostly.


00:48:16.685 --> 00:48:19.177
Once they are at peace,
then they can move on.


00:48:19.271 --> 00:48:21.684
We can tear down their room
and then we start again.


00:48:22.608 --> 00:48:25.396
And are there those that
don't react so favorably?


00:48:27.113 --> 00:48:28.570
Yes.


00:48:28.656 --> 00:48:31.148
Yes, we lock them away.


00:48:31.242 --> 00:48:33.279
How does one lock a spirit away?


00:48:33.369 --> 00:48:36.032
Thirteen nails seals them in.


00:48:36.122 --> 00:48:38.956
Once they find peace, we can
release them and they can


00:48:39.041 --> 00:48:40.452
leave this house.


00:48:40.543 --> 00:48:43.877
So thirteen is a devilish number
to protect you from devils?


00:48:43.963 --> 00:48:46.125
No, no, no.
That is a divine number,


00:48:46.215 --> 00:48:49.424
to protect the cycle
of life and death.


00:48:49.510 --> 00:48:51.502
And does this divine
number always work?


00:48:51.595 --> 00:48:55.088
I mean what if a spirit simply
doesn't want to be locked away?


00:48:56.892 --> 00:49:01.978
The unmendable souls prey upon
the innocent and the pure.


00:49:03.232 --> 00:49:05.440
And by the innocent and
pure, you mean Master Henry?


00:49:08.737 --> 00:49:10.649
We can stand between them.


00:49:10.739 --> 00:49:13.072
I and you.


00:49:14.410 --> 00:49:17.699
With your assistance, I can
help this spirit find peace.


00:49:23.627 --> 00:49:26.290
You don't believe
any of this. I understand.


00:49:26.380 --> 00:49:27.712
Ma'am, I do not.


00:49:27.798 --> 00:49:32.463
I do not believe in anything
I cannot see or study.


00:49:33.637 --> 00:49:36.505
Mrs Winchester, you have built
this house, th-this place,


00:49:36.599 --> 00:49:39.558
this reality. Therefore, you
can control it, can you not?


00:49:40.436 --> 00:49:42.098
Yes, perhaps.


00:49:42.688 --> 00:49:45.101
We all have the ability
to create and control


00:49:45.191 --> 00:49:47.854
our own reality. But for some,
for you, Mrs Winchester,


00:49:47.943 --> 00:49:51.232
for you, that will
mean letting go of the past.


00:49:52.781 --> 00:49:54.738
Make your assessment, doctor.


00:49:56.827 --> 00:50:00.366
Say what you feel is the
truth about Sarah Winchester.


00:50:01.499 --> 00:50:04.207
And if that means you lose
control of your company?


00:50:04.293 --> 00:50:05.659
Oh!


00:50:05.753 --> 00:50:08.666
There are worse things in this
world to lose than that, doctor.


00:50:16.138 --> 00:50:17.754
I see you've finished
the new room.


00:50:17.848 --> 00:50:19.931
Of course.


00:50:20.518 --> 00:50:22.851
Must be very
profitable for you,


00:50:23.729 --> 00:50:25.311
all this working
round the clock.


00:50:26.106 --> 00:50:29.565
We all appreciate Mrs
Winchester's ongoing employment,


00:50:29.652 --> 00:50:32.315
and her creativity.


00:50:33.572 --> 00:50:35.905
I must say, that creativity
certainly leads to some


00:50:35.991 --> 00:50:37.323
rather odd designs.


00:50:38.369 --> 00:50:40.577
Do you think it possible a
woman of advancing years may be


00:50:40.663 --> 00:50:43.155
susceptible to flights of fancy?


00:50:43.249 --> 00:50:44.911
No, sir.


00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:46.411
I do not.


00:50:49.505 --> 00:50:52.213
Could I see inside the
garden room, please?


00:50:52.299 --> 00:50:54.461
I had one similar
and I would be much obliged...


00:50:54.552 --> 00:50:57.135
No, sir.
That room is sealed.


00:50:57.221 --> 00:50:59.713
Therefore it's off limits.


00:51:00.224 --> 00:51:02.136
Good day, doctor.


00:51:07.147 --> 00:51:09.434
Well, Eric, that's
going really well.


00:51:24.081 --> 00:51:25.117
How is he?


00:51:26.584 --> 00:51:28.166
Fine.
Resting.


00:51:28.252 --> 00:51:31.290
Has he ever been prone to
behavior like that in the past?


00:51:32.256 --> 00:51:33.292
No.


00:51:33.382 --> 00:51:34.714
Never?


00:51:37.219 --> 00:51:40.678
She told you, didn't she,
about the Winchester curse?


00:51:41.599 --> 00:51:42.635
Yes.


00:51:42.725 --> 00:51:45.559
Do you believe her, or
do you think she's crazy?


00:51:45.644 --> 00:51:48.557
I think crazy is
a dangerous word.


00:51:49.523 --> 00:51:52.857
People have certain medical
conditions and with the right


00:51:52.943 --> 00:51:55.060
diagnosis and treatment,
they can be helped.


00:51:59.950 --> 00:52:02.408
I do not believe
in curses, doctor.


00:52:02.494 --> 00:52:06.909
Good. Nor do I. I think
perhaps your son's behavior


00:52:06.999 --> 00:52:09.787
has been triggered by the
sudden death of his father.


00:52:10.336 --> 00:52:11.872
Yes.


00:52:11.962 --> 00:52:14.955
Could you tell me how
your husband died?


00:52:15.049 --> 00:52:21.171
He had demons, but not the kind
that my aunt believes haunt her.


00:52:24.391 --> 00:52:25.632
Go on.


00:52:25.726 --> 00:52:29.845
Aunt Sarah's husband died
suddenly of tuberculosis.


00:52:29.938 --> 00:52:32.555
And then she lost poor Annie.


00:52:34.026 --> 00:52:37.360
She believes our family
curse is spreading.


00:52:46.914 --> 00:52:50.874
My, my husband loved the drink
more than his wife and child.


00:52:51.669 --> 00:52:53.752
I believe that was his curse.


00:52:55.547 --> 00:53:00.167
Now he is gone,
and I'm alone,


00:53:00.260 --> 00:53:02.718
better off in so
many ways without him.


00:53:03.681 --> 00:53:05.388
But it terrifies me.


00:53:05.474 --> 00:53:07.807
Don't let that fear control you.


00:53:08.686 --> 00:53:11.554
Hey, fear only
exists in your mind.


00:53:12.690 --> 00:53:15.524
When we fear the most,
we must take control.


00:53:17.319 --> 00:53:19.936
You can be a fighter.
You can be a protector.


00:53:20.030 --> 00:53:22.147
I do not feel like a protector.


00:53:23.200 --> 00:53:25.192
Aunt Sarah is the fighter.


00:53:25.744 --> 00:53:26.825
Yes.


00:53:26.912 --> 00:53:28.824
She would die to save us.


00:53:28.914 --> 00:53:30.371
Perhaps.


00:53:30.457 --> 00:53:33.825
Have you ever loved someone so
much you would die to save them?


00:53:35.879 --> 00:53:37.211
I have.


00:53:38.507 --> 00:53:42.842
I also knew someone who was
haunted by demons, voices.


00:53:44.179 --> 00:53:47.047
And did the time ever come
when you had to protect them?


00:53:47.599 --> 00:53:49.010
It did.


00:53:50.936 --> 00:53:52.677
What did you do?


00:53:53.897 --> 00:53:55.763
I died.


00:54:21.133 --> 00:54:22.419
Henry!


00:54:22.509 --> 00:54:24.466
Ohhh!


00:54:28.515 --> 00:54:29.175
Henry!


00:54:30.184 --> 00:54:30.970
Henry!


00:54:31.059 --> 00:54:32.595
Ohhh!


00:54:46.158 --> 00:54:47.114
Henry!


00:54:47.201 --> 00:54:49.659
Henry! It's me!


00:54:51.497 --> 00:54:53.079
Oh!


00:55:17.231 --> 00:55:18.472
No!


00:55:19.650 --> 00:55:21.061
Ohhh!


00:55:27.115 --> 00:55:29.232
Henry! Henry!


00:55:30.869 --> 00:55:32.451
Stop it! Stop!


00:55:33.580 --> 00:55:34.696
Stop Henry, stop!


00:55:34.790 --> 00:55:35.951
Who are you?


00:55:36.041 --> 00:55:37.577
Die!


00:55:48.262 --> 00:55:49.673
M-Mother?


00:55:51.974 --> 00:55:53.385
Oh Henry!


00:56:03.068 --> 00:56:04.775
I'm so sorry, Aunt Sarah.


00:56:04.862 --> 00:56:06.273
I've let you down and
I've let Henry down.


00:56:06.363 --> 00:56:07.854
No, no.


00:56:08.866 --> 00:56:11.483
This spirit has a power
we've not seen before.


00:56:11.869 --> 00:56:13.280
Oh my god!


00:56:13.370 --> 00:56:16.033
It can take over a mind.


00:56:18.750 --> 00:56:20.912
John, send everyone home.


00:56:21.003 --> 00:56:22.995
Only we in this
room must remain.


00:56:23.088 --> 00:56:24.295
Yes, Ma'am.


00:56:24.381 --> 00:56:26.748
This child must be taken
to a hospital immediately.


00:56:26.842 --> 00:56:28.333
No, no.
We must watch over him...


00:56:28.427 --> 00:56:29.668
To a hospital immediately.


00:56:29.761 --> 00:56:31.798
No. No-one else will
understand. He must stay here.


00:56:31.889 --> 00:56:33.130
- This is insanity.
- We will watch over him.


00:56:33.223 --> 00:56:34.589
Dr Price may be right.


00:56:36.184 --> 00:56:38.346
No. No.
We will protect him.


00:56:38.437 --> 00:56:40.099
We will protect
him at all costs.


00:56:40.188 --> 00:56:41.019
John, come with me.


00:56:41.106 --> 00:56:42.017
Aunt Sarah!


00:56:42.941 --> 00:56:44.307
Oohh!


00:56:44.401 --> 00:56:47.018
Ma'am, I insist that you
receive medical treatment.


00:56:47.112 --> 00:56:48.398
Seal that door.


00:56:48.488 --> 00:56:50.150
Thirteen nails.


00:56:50.240 --> 00:56:51.356
Now.


00:56:51.950 --> 00:56:53.031
Now!


00:56:54.244 --> 00:56:55.655
Yes, Ma'am.


00:57:00.292 --> 00:57:02.409
You leave my family alone.


00:57:04.546 --> 00:57:06.378
You speak with me.


00:57:14.181 --> 00:57:15.592
Let's just think this through.


00:57:15.682 --> 00:57:17.765
Please, Mrs Marriott,
be rational.


00:57:17.851 --> 00:57:20.468
Henry clearly has a
trauma and needs help.


00:57:20.562 --> 00:57:22.053
Your aunt is caught
in a superstition.


00:57:22.147 --> 00:57:24.264
We need-


00:58:11.488 --> 00:58:13.229
Thirteen hooks.


00:58:13.323 --> 00:58:14.939
You must listen to me.


00:58:15.033 --> 00:58:16.899
Is the rifle room finished?


00:58:16.994 --> 00:58:18.280
Yes, Ma'am.


00:58:18.370 --> 00:58:20.612
My god!
This presence is so strong.


00:58:20.706 --> 00:58:22.493
Oh, I feel its hatred...


00:58:22.582 --> 00:58:23.914
Oh, enough with the games!


00:58:24.001 --> 00:58:25.708
We're taking this
boy to a hospital.


00:58:25.794 --> 00:58:26.659
We should listen to him.


00:58:26.753 --> 00:58:28.585
Yes! The boy tried to kill you!


00:58:28.672 --> 00:58:32.131
No! The shadows will follow us.
Wherever we go.


00:58:32.217 --> 00:58:35.551
No, Henry will not
suffer the same fate...


00:58:35.637 --> 00:58:37.594
Henry's condition cannot
be cured by witchcraft.


00:58:37.681 --> 00:58:38.842
The boy needs a doctor.


00:58:38.932 --> 00:58:41.299
Conditions can be cured, doctor.


00:58:41.393 --> 00:58:43.225
Curses cannot.


00:58:43.311 --> 00:58:44.472
Mrs Marriott,
will you listen to me?


00:58:44.563 --> 00:58:45.428
Marion!


00:58:45.522 --> 00:58:46.603
I'm, I'm, I'm going
with Dr Price!


00:58:46.690 --> 00:58:47.851
No! Henry must stay!


00:58:47.941 --> 00:58:49.102
I'll make the arrangements.


00:58:49.192 --> 00:58:50.558
Gentlemen, you'll excuse me.


00:58:50.652 --> 00:58:52.769
No! No! Marion,
please! Henry must stay.


00:58:52.863 --> 00:58:53.899
He must stay with us.


00:58:53.989 --> 00:58:55.651
Aunt Sarah, I must
think of Henry.


00:58:55.741 --> 00:58:57.323
I should go with him.


00:58:57.409 --> 00:58:58.991
I will prove it to you.


00:59:01.038 --> 00:59:02.995
Yes, I, I will.


00:59:03.665 --> 00:59:04.951
This way.


00:59:21.767 --> 00:59:22.803
Operator.


00:59:25.729 --> 00:59:27.311
Winchester
Repeating Arms Company.


00:59:27.397 --> 00:59:28.387
This is Arthur Gates.


00:59:28.482 --> 00:59:31.475
Mr Gates, it's
Dr Eric Price here.


00:59:32.444 --> 00:59:34.936
Oh, I trust the assessment
is going well, doctor.


00:59:35.030 --> 00:59:37.272
I understand you
received our letter.


00:59:37.365 --> 00:59:39.573
It's fine, Mr Gates.
But I require immediate


00:59:39.659 --> 00:59:42.117
transportation
to the nearest hospital.


00:59:42.204 --> 00:59:43.445
Is everything alright?


00:59:43.538 --> 00:59:44.574
Everything is fine.


00:59:44.664 --> 00:59:46.155
Just please, a driver,
as soon as possible.


00:59:46.249 --> 00:59:48.286
Of course, right away.
- Thank you.


00:59:48.376 --> 00:59:50.584
And ah the assessment, doctor?


00:59:50.670 --> 00:59:52.457
You'll get what you wanted.


00:59:53.632 --> 00:59:55.043
Christ!


00:59:59.179 --> 01:00:01.421
I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to be rude.


01:00:01.515 --> 01:00:05.225
Sir, we're all deeply concerned
for Master Henry's wellbeing.


01:00:05.310 --> 01:00:07.597
If there is anything
I can do to assist you, I...


01:00:08.647 --> 01:00:11.139
Well, actually you can.


01:00:11.233 --> 01:00:13.099
I need to get my bags, please?


01:00:13.193 --> 01:00:14.354
Of course.


01:00:14.444 --> 01:00:17.187
- Thank you.
- Happy to help.


01:00:18.156 --> 01:00:19.272
Hmmm.


01:00:21.743 --> 01:00:24.861
Mrs Winchester is
truly a remarkable woman.


01:00:24.955 --> 01:00:28.244
She knows what she's doing.
She has created a vessel


01:00:28.333 --> 01:00:30.370
for the deceased to
communicate with her.


01:00:30.460 --> 01:00:32.247
She's certainly created some
architectural oddities.


01:00:32.337 --> 01:00:35.455
This house, I've seen things.


01:00:37.884 --> 01:00:39.967
I know this room.


01:00:40.762 --> 01:00:41.718
Things?


01:00:42.931 --> 01:00:44.263
The dead.


01:00:45.600 --> 01:00:46.886
Criminals.


01:00:47.769 --> 01:00:49.852
Lost souls who
met a violent end.


01:00:53.650 --> 01:00:56.518
You've seen them, haven't you?


01:01:03.743 --> 01:01:06.907
Dr Price, many staff have
reported hearing noises.


01:01:06.997 --> 01:01:09.865
They come from inside rooms
that have been nailed shut.


01:01:09.958 --> 01:01:13.326
Strange occurrences in those
rooms; that is why the doors


01:01:13.420 --> 01:01:15.503
have been sealed, to
keep the unruly in.


01:01:15.589 --> 01:01:18.297
But the staff have
only heard noises.


01:01:18.383 --> 01:01:22.593
To see them, well, I believe
you and I are unique.


01:01:23.597 --> 01:01:24.804
Really?


01:01:26.141 --> 01:01:27.973
Yes, perhaps it's all just a
symptom of Mrs Winchester's


01:01:28.059 --> 01:01:29.641
persuasive influence.


01:01:29.728 --> 01:01:33.438
Sir, locking Mrs Marriott
and her child away is only


01:01:33.523 --> 01:01:34.980
delaying the inevitable.


01:01:35.942 --> 01:01:37.023
And what is the inevitable?


01:01:37.110 --> 01:01:39.853
They're all Winchester.
They will all-


01:01:39.946 --> 01:01:41.437
die.


01:02:08.391 --> 01:02:09.347
Mr Hansen!


01:02:09.434 --> 01:02:10.470
Is she in there?


01:02:10.560 --> 01:02:11.971
Yes, doctor.


01:02:12.062 --> 01:02:14.429
Good. You need to hear this.
Mrs Winchester, there is a man


01:02:14.522 --> 01:02:17.265
in your employ who has
clearly lost his mind. He just...


01:02:19.110 --> 01:02:20.317
That's him!


01:02:20.403 --> 01:02:21.610
You saw him?


01:02:21.696 --> 01:02:22.903
You spoke with him?


01:02:22.989 --> 01:02:24.230
Well, yes, I spoke
with him just now.


01:02:24.324 --> 01:02:25.440
The man threatened you.


01:02:25.533 --> 01:02:27.320
Read it.
Read the paper.


01:02:30.413 --> 01:02:33.622
'Corporal Benjamin Joseph Block
was killed during a siege at


01:02:33.708 --> 01:02:35.665
the Winchester Repeating
Arms general office.'


01:02:35.752 --> 01:02:36.617
That's impossible.


01:02:36.711 --> 01:02:39.078
This newspaper
is 20 years old.


01:02:41.424 --> 01:02:45.213
Cruelty, grief and loss can make
people do unimaginable things.


01:02:49.933 --> 01:02:52.266
Ben lost two brothers
on the battlefield.


01:02:52.352 --> 01:02:54.765
The youngest was
only 14 years old.


01:02:55.939 --> 01:02:58.431
Their confederate muskets were
no match for the Winchester


01:02:58.525 --> 01:03:00.892
rifles of the Union Army.


01:03:01.486 --> 01:03:03.148
They were cut down.


01:03:09.703 --> 01:03:11.194
Ben swore revenge.


01:03:12.831 --> 01:03:14.993
To him, the people who created
the weapon that killed his


01:03:15.083 --> 01:03:18.827
brothers were as guilty as
those who pulled the trigger.


01:03:28.972 --> 01:03:31.965
He killed fifteen
innocent people that day.


01:03:33.310 --> 01:03:35.347
He locked himself
in the display room.


01:03:35.437 --> 01:03:37.599
We used to call it
the show-off room.


01:03:39.399 --> 01:03:42.107
We know you're in there.
We have the building surrounded.


01:03:55.081 --> 01:03:56.868
Officer John
Mandel told the press


01:03:56.958 --> 01:03:59.541
'I'm extremely proud of my
team, and that scum like Block


01:03:59.627 --> 01:04:01.539
can't escape my men
and their Winchesters'.


01:04:01.629 --> 01:04:02.836
Weapons ready!


01:04:23.151 --> 01:04:24.232
This way.


01:04:24.319 --> 01:04:26.060
When the bell
chimes at midnight,


01:04:26.154 --> 01:04:28.362
he'll be at his most powerful.


01:04:29.491 --> 01:04:32.859
Do you know who the most
terrifying monster is, doctor?


01:04:33.536 --> 01:04:34.572
No.


01:04:36.247 --> 01:04:38.705
The one you invite
into your own home.


01:04:50.720 --> 01:04:51.961
This is it.


01:04:54.724 --> 01:04:56.306
This is the room.


01:05:15.412 --> 01:05:18.746
This is an exact replica of
the room he was killed in.


01:05:19.249 --> 01:05:20.660
Yes.


01:05:20.750 --> 01:05:24.118
And now that it is complete,
he is in this world.


01:05:25.046 --> 01:05:27.288
Do you see anyone, doctor?


01:05:28.508 --> 01:05:29.669
It's impossible.


01:05:29.759 --> 01:05:32.046
Doctor, you must believe.


01:05:32.679 --> 01:05:34.341
It's illogical.


01:05:44.691 --> 01:05:47.399
Corporal Block, please,


01:05:49.654 --> 01:05:52.738
please feel my deep remorse


01:05:52.824 --> 01:05:55.191
for the death
of your brothers,


01:05:55.827 --> 01:05:59.366
of James and young Harry


01:05:59.456 --> 01:06:01.539
by the Winchester rifle.


01:06:01.624 --> 01:06:05.664
I know all three of you
feel pain and torment.


01:06:06.713 --> 01:06:09.046
But violence cannot
bring justice.


01:06:10.341 --> 01:06:13.459
Only more suffering,
and I will not allow my family


01:06:13.553 --> 01:06:15.545
to suffer any more.


01:06:17.640 --> 01:06:19.927
Leave this house
with your brothers.


01:06:20.977 --> 01:06:23.560
I hope together
you can find peace.


01:06:33.323 --> 01:06:36.987
Beautiful dreamer,
wake unto me;


01:07:20.328 --> 01:07:21.694
It's Ben.


01:08:14.799 --> 01:08:15.835
Stop them!


01:08:22.140 --> 01:08:23.005
No!


01:08:53.254 --> 01:08:54.620
Mrs Winchester?


01:08:59.677 --> 01:09:02.010
Oh! I'll find
another way to get to you!


01:09:13.524 --> 01:09:15.811
Henry,
sweetheart, where are you?


01:09:18.946 --> 01:09:19.936
Henry?


01:09:20.323 --> 01:09:21.404
Henry?


01:09:29.707 --> 01:09:30.618
Henry!


01:09:32.585 --> 01:09:34.201
Henry! Henry!


01:09:45.682 --> 01:09:48.265
Eric, this is just in your mind.
Fear is just in your mind.


01:09:48.351 --> 01:09:50.263
It is only in your mind.


01:10:33.563 --> 01:10:34.929
Henry?


01:10:42.905 --> 01:10:44.441
Henry, where are you?


01:10:51.664 --> 01:10:53.155
Henry, sweetheart?


01:10:53.624 --> 01:10:55.456
Where are you?


01:11:18.941 --> 01:11:21.399
Be free, my brothers.


01:12:10.701 --> 01:12:13.489
I always loved our
garden room, sweetheart.


01:12:14.372 --> 01:12:15.829
Ruby!


01:12:15.915 --> 01:12:18.123
But you let it die!


01:12:18.209 --> 01:12:19.120
Oh no.


01:12:20.378 --> 01:12:23.962
Tell me the story about the
farmer, who owned the old mule.


01:12:24.048 --> 01:12:24.913
No.


01:12:25.007 --> 01:12:27.340
I always liked that story.


01:12:27.885 --> 01:12:30.002
They built our garden room.


01:12:31.097 --> 01:12:34.261
The farmer's old mule
fell into his well.


01:12:35.852 --> 01:12:37.218
Go on, Eric.


01:12:39.021 --> 01:12:40.432
The farmer heard...


01:12:42.525 --> 01:12:44.767
He heard the mule crying.


01:12:46.070 --> 01:12:47.652
And it broke his heart.


01:12:48.990 --> 01:12:51.698
He chose to bury the animal in
the well and put it out of its...


01:12:51.784 --> 01:12:53.070
its hardship.


01:12:53.828 --> 01:12:55.911
He started shoveling.


01:12:57.248 --> 01:13:01.242
The mule realized that every
time dirt fell on his back, he


01:13:01.335 --> 01:13:04.419
could shake it off and step up.


01:13:05.047 --> 01:13:06.208
Shovel after shovel.


01:13:06.299 --> 01:13:08.507
He could shake it off
and he could step up...


01:13:08.593 --> 01:13:10.050
Shake it off.


01:13:10.136 --> 01:13:14.676
It wasn't long before the old
mule, battered and exhausted,


01:13:14.765 --> 01:13:17.599
stepped over the
wall of that well.


01:13:18.561 --> 01:13:20.302
What should have buried him...


01:13:21.522 --> 01:13:22.933
Saved him.


01:13:23.024 --> 01:13:24.435
And he overcame...


01:13:24.525 --> 01:13:26.016
This is not real.


01:13:26.110 --> 01:13:27.772
This is not happening.
You are not real.


01:13:27.862 --> 01:13:29.603
I've tried to be a good wife.


01:13:29.697 --> 01:13:31.734
The voices are not real, Ruby.


01:13:31.824 --> 01:13:34.191
They were never real.
They were just inside your head.


01:13:34.285 --> 01:13:37.153
All these years, all I wanted
was for you to believe me but...


01:13:37.246 --> 01:13:39.659
- I should have put you in care.
- You never did.


01:13:39.749 --> 01:13:40.990
I should have put you in care.


01:13:41.083 --> 01:13:43.666
Just something that can
be diagnosed and treated,


01:13:43.753 --> 01:13:45.460
like any other crazy person.


01:13:45.546 --> 01:13:47.754
Yes. I did.
I made a mistake.


01:13:47.840 --> 01:13:48.705
I'm sorry.


01:13:48.799 --> 01:13:51.917
A delusional disorder.
- Yes.


01:13:52.011 --> 01:13:53.627
That's what you called it.
- Yes.


01:13:53.721 --> 01:13:56.338
Put the gun down, Ruby, please.
We can talk about this.


01:13:56.432 --> 01:13:58.549
I don't want to talk anymore.


01:13:58.643 --> 01:14:00.930
I need you to believe me.


01:14:01.020 --> 01:14:03.307
I don't know what
I believe anymore.


01:14:04.649 --> 01:14:06.766
Someone like you never will.


01:14:07.234 --> 01:14:08.520
Please, Ruby, don't.


01:14:08.611 --> 01:14:10.568
Please, I'm lost
without you, Ruby.


01:14:10.655 --> 01:14:12.772
I'm lost without you.


01:14:12.865 --> 01:14:14.606
Don't do it. No!


01:14:44.188 --> 01:14:45.724
You can go on.


01:14:46.816 --> 01:14:49.479
You need to let
go of your guilt,


01:14:51.612 --> 01:14:53.729
so that I can let go of mine,


01:14:54.699 --> 01:14:57.112
and see the truth.


01:15:02.498 --> 01:15:04.330
I'm so sorry.


01:16:59.907 --> 01:17:01.990
Mrs Winchester, are you alright?


01:17:02.827 --> 01:17:06.286
This spirit is destroying
the balance of this house.


01:17:08.624 --> 01:17:10.616
It has to be stopped.


01:17:16.799 --> 01:17:19.382
Master Henry and Marion,
we need to find them.


01:17:20.386 --> 01:17:21.968
Seal that door.


01:17:23.389 --> 01:17:25.506
Ben must not leave.


01:17:31.981 --> 01:17:33.267
Henry?


01:18:16.400 --> 01:18:17.561
Thirteen.


01:18:18.194 --> 01:18:19.230
Sit.


01:18:23.657 --> 01:18:25.398
Sarah, I can see them.


01:18:25.492 --> 01:18:27.575
I can see all of them.


01:18:27.661 --> 01:18:29.618
You're the only one who can.


01:18:30.706 --> 01:18:31.992
You believe?


01:18:32.082 --> 01:18:33.163
I do.


01:18:33.876 --> 01:18:35.117
I do.


01:18:35.211 --> 01:18:39.501
Dead for three minutes, killed
by the Winchester rifle.


01:18:40.466 --> 01:18:42.628
You are connected to this house.


01:18:44.053 --> 01:18:45.294
Yes.


01:18:52.895 --> 01:18:54.011
Henry!


01:18:56.398 --> 01:18:57.605
I'm not afraid.


01:19:03.989 --> 01:19:05.821
I'm not afraid.


01:19:08.160 --> 01:19:11.028
I, I won't let fear control me.


01:19:20.923 --> 01:19:21.913
Henry!


01:19:23.425 --> 01:19:24.757
Henry!


01:19:28.305 --> 01:19:30.513
Oh please, please
come back to me!


01:19:39.108 --> 01:19:41.942
Marion and Henry
are in grave danger.


01:19:42.027 --> 01:19:46.488
The only way to save them
is to stop Ben here and now.


01:19:49.368 --> 01:19:51.781
Ben, leave my family alone.


01:19:55.165 --> 01:19:56.997
You speak to me.


01:19:58.961 --> 01:20:00.577
Talk to me...


01:20:03.632 --> 01:20:04.873
now.


01:20:14.977 --> 01:20:16.058
Sarah!


01:20:17.813 --> 01:20:20.100
Corporal Block is in this room.


01:20:25.446 --> 01:20:27.733
Winchesters are a vile plague!


01:20:27.823 --> 01:20:29.985
This whore bitch has to die!


01:20:30.075 --> 01:20:30.986
Sarah, fight him!


01:20:31.952 --> 01:20:34.444
My brothers were killed by
the rifle, murdered by this


01:20:34.538 --> 01:20:36.245
instrument of death...


01:20:36.332 --> 01:20:36.947
Fight him!


01:20:37.041 --> 01:20:38.907
...that killed your wife.


01:20:44.006 --> 01:20:45.668
Sarah, control this!
Control it!


01:20:46.759 --> 01:20:48.216
Be present, Sarah!
Be present.


01:20:48.302 --> 01:20:49.588
I want you to suffer.


01:20:50.596 --> 01:20:51.803
Marion is mine.


01:20:51.889 --> 01:20:53.471
Henry is mine!


01:20:53.557 --> 01:20:55.799
- Sarah, no! Fight it!
- An eye for an eye!


01:20:55.893 --> 01:20:57.304
Get off me!


01:20:57.394 --> 01:20:59.977
These vermin profit from death.


01:21:00.064 --> 01:21:00.975
Sarah, fight him!


01:21:01.065 --> 01:21:02.226
No more!


01:21:08.197 --> 01:21:10.940
Oh! Seal the floor, doctor.


01:21:11.033 --> 01:21:13.070
Thirteen nails. Hurry!


01:21:14.870 --> 01:21:16.736
His rage is endless.


01:21:18.248 --> 01:21:19.489
But he can be stopped.


01:21:19.583 --> 01:21:20.494
How?


01:21:20.584 --> 01:21:23.702
By something,
something in this room.


01:21:24.296 --> 01:21:25.878
He's afraid of something.


01:21:25.964 --> 01:21:27.250
I felt it.


01:21:30.177 --> 01:21:31.418
His gun!


01:21:33.138 --> 01:21:34.219
That's twelve!


01:21:35.474 --> 01:21:36.590
This is the gun...


01:21:40.437 --> 01:21:42.099
he used to kill.


01:21:47.736 --> 01:21:49.022
Do you see him?


01:21:49.113 --> 01:21:49.944
No.


01:21:51.448 --> 01:21:53.280
There. Done!


01:21:53.367 --> 01:21:54.699
Now he's locked in.


01:21:54.785 --> 01:21:56.651
And so are we.


01:22:06.547 --> 01:22:08.789
Ben, show yourself.


01:22:11.176 --> 01:22:12.883
Show yourself!


01:22:47.296 --> 01:22:50.630
Your anger will never defeat us.


01:23:11.653 --> 01:23:13.861
You took
everything from me!


01:23:13.947 --> 01:23:15.188
Ahhh!


01:23:22.289 --> 01:23:23.621
They're going
right through him!


01:23:23.707 --> 01:23:24.993
You saw him?


01:23:25.083 --> 01:23:25.914
Yes!


01:23:40.015 --> 01:23:41.051
Who's there?


01:23:42.684 --> 01:23:44.050
You're there.


01:23:44.144 --> 01:23:46.557
You are there amongst the dead.


01:23:47.689 --> 01:23:49.055
It's not the gun.


01:23:49.149 --> 01:23:51.766
He's afraid of something else.


01:24:00.494 --> 01:24:03.032
You kept it and refurbished it.


01:24:03.539 --> 01:24:05.451
All because it's a
reminder of my past.


01:24:05.541 --> 01:24:08.329
Instruments of death
have a powerful connection


01:24:08.418 --> 01:24:10.034
to the afterlife.


01:24:11.255 --> 01:24:14.464
What should have
killed him, saved him.


01:24:25.185 --> 01:24:28.428
Ben, we can help you be
free of your torment.


01:24:35.279 --> 01:24:36.611
I'm a mother...


01:24:42.536 --> 01:24:43.777
a fighter.


01:24:47.499 --> 01:24:48.740
Show yourself.


01:24:51.587 --> 01:24:52.828
A protector.


01:24:54.881 --> 01:24:57.168
And I am not afraid.


01:25:52.731 --> 01:25:54.313
See the truth.


01:26:19.216 --> 01:26:20.377
Yes!


01:26:29.017 --> 01:26:30.349
He's at peace.


01:26:31.853 --> 01:26:33.594
He has joined his brothers.


01:26:34.189 --> 01:26:35.930
You've done it.


01:26:36.024 --> 01:26:37.140
They're gone.


01:26:42.155 --> 01:26:45.193
Everybody else,
go back to your rooms-


01:26:47.994 --> 01:26:49.451
all of you.


01:27:15.021 --> 01:27:16.478
Oh! Henry!


01:27:17.983 --> 01:27:18.643
Henry!


01:27:19.693 --> 01:27:21.855
Henry!
Oh, Henry!


01:27:27.325 --> 01:27:31.319
Dear Mr Gates, below you will
find my psychological assessment


01:27:31.413 --> 01:27:35.498
and mental status examination of
Mrs Sarah Lockwood Winchester.


01:27:36.918 --> 01:27:39.376
It was conducted at her home
between the dates of April 12 to


01:27:39.463 --> 01:27:44.254
April 19, 1906, and prepared at
the request of the Winchester


01:27:44.342 --> 01:27:48.382
Repeating Arms Company.
In my professional opinion,


01:27:48.472 --> 01:27:51.590
after having observed Mrs
Winchester for the past week,


01:27:51.683 --> 01:27:56.053
it is my conclusion that she is
of sound mind and body, and is


01:27:56.146 --> 01:27:59.105
fit to continue in her role with
the Winchester Repeating Arms


01:27:59.191 --> 01:28:02.935
Company, for as long as
she desires such a burden.


01:28:08.033 --> 01:28:10.946
Yours truly, Dr Eric A Price.


01:28:28.094 --> 01:28:30.711
It's time for us both
to leave this house.


01:28:33.975 --> 01:28:35.432
I'll always miss you.


01:28:51.535 --> 01:28:54.198
Thank you, Dr Price,
for your help.


01:28:55.163 --> 01:28:56.119
Young man.


01:29:00.001 --> 01:29:01.287
Thank you.


01:29:15.141 --> 01:29:16.803
Time for me to say goodbye.


01:29:25.944 --> 01:29:27.606
Ruby loves you.


01:29:29.072 --> 01:29:31.280
That did not stop
after her death.


01:29:32.033 --> 01:29:34.070
You know that, don't you?


01:29:35.161 --> 01:29:36.618
I do.


01:29:41.751 --> 01:29:44.789
You know, in spite of
everything, you really-


01:29:45.922 --> 01:29:47.914
do have a beautiful home.


01:29:48.341 --> 01:29:50.173
What are you going to next?


01:29:51.511 --> 01:29:53.468
Rebuild, of course.


01:29:55.682 --> 01:29:57.014
Of course.

